================================================================================
Third-party components (INVENTORY INCOMPLETE — see item 2 above)
================================================================================

The desktop application distributes third-party software in binary form. This
is redistribution, not mere use, so each component's license terms apply to
the distributed artifacts.

Components known to be redistributed:

  * Electron and its bundled Chromium/Node.js runtime
      -> shipped in the packaged .dmg / .exe

  * The Python dependency tree frozen into the backend sidecar by PyInstaller
      -> see agentic-cli/pyproject.toml and dashboard/backend for the roots

  * PyInstaller bootloader code embedded in the frozen binary
      -> PyInstaller's license carries an exception governing the terms under
         which frozen applications may be distributed; confirm its current
         wording applies to this project's distribution model

Components NOT redistributed (referenced or downloaded at runtime, not shipped
in the installer):

  * Neo4j — referenced via docker-compose; the user supplies the server
  * The optional built-in language model — downloaded on first use into
    ~/.keel/models at the user's request; nothing ships in the installer

Each entry above still requires its license confirmed and recorded. Where a
dependency's own license requires attribution, reproduce its NOTICE content
here.
